fix: self-only adopted stop (cross-instance safety) + deferred self-kill + card cleanup

- adopted-stop now only ever targets the current process: the PID record is
  shared state across dsh instances, and a second profile-web instance (e.g.
  on another port, whose plugin config still says the default port) could stop
  the main harness through it — observed in testing. status.stoppable and
  stop() both require the recorded PID to be process.pid.
- the self-kill is deferred (~800ms) so the HTTP response flushes before the
  process dies — Stop on the launcher server no longer surfaces
  "Failed to fetch".
- dispose() no longer stops the adopted server: a plugin reload must not take
  the harness down (the launcher server hosts the plugin).
- settings card: the Start button is removed (the card is served by the web
  itself, so it is always listening — start lives in the tools/command), and
  a failed fetch on Stop/Open is reported as the action having been
  dispatched instead of a scary error.
